WEBVTT

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.520
I’ll be working here with you in
Kawachi’s stead from now on.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.440
I’m Kanmuri Shigeru.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.740
Let’s all get along.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.530
If Kanmuri-kun’s a hard worker, then hip hip hurrah.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.320
Because self-replication is tiring.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.620
Kanmuri,

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.340
why did you choose to come
here instead of the Main Branch?

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.510
In order to beat Azusagawa Yukino,

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.340
there’s no longer any choice but to fight from this store.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.670
Pantasia’s Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.970
Correctly speaking,

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.890
this store is leased under your
name, Azusagawa Tsukino, right?

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.720
Yes, Grandfather had arranged it that way.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.270
That’s right.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.770
Therefore, even in the worst possible scenario,

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.730
this store alone can do what it pleases.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.650
In the worst possible scenario, you say?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.910
If Pantasia is taken over by St. Pierre, I mean.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.370
Azusagawa Yukino is conspiring with St. Pierre

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.760
and has acquired up to 40% of Pantasia’s stock.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.420
A takeover is now merely a matter of time.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.170
What was that?!

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:12.550
Manager!

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.800
Is “What was that?!” okay in this instance?

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.970
Right now, such a thing doesn’t matter one tiny bit.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.390
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.270
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.560
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.890
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:34.200
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.870
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:55.100
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:03.070
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:10.940
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:18.660
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:26.130
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:35.510
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:44.270
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.530
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.520
is the light of only you.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.270
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:55.270 --> 00:03:00.080
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:07.800
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.850
The ten billion yen man!?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.810
Pantasia’s life or death crisis!

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.380
Dammit!

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.610
I was finally...

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.890
I was finally able to make it to the Main Branch...

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.410
Well, I suppose it’s nice having a chandelier...

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.150
And the room I’m boarding in is nice and big...

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.950
Normally, I’d be celebrating...

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.460
But, I can’t under these circumstances, even for a
tiny bit, thanks to a single word from that moron.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.000
Man, it’s looking bad.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:40.960
It’s gonna be really hard.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.760
It’s Pantasia’s greatest crisis!

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.460
Kawachi-san.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.670
I’ve brought breakfast.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.680
What’s with this gorgeous food being catered for me?

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.510
I don’t even know how to eat this.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.670
I mean, it looks like the kind of thing
that might produce a “reaction” out of me.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.310
Come to think of it...

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.490
It’s been a while since I’ve had
breakfast that was made by someone else.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.690
Since Azuma was no good
at making anything but bread,

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.320
it was always me preparing it.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.820
It’s delicious, Kawachi!

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.690
Don’t talk with food in your mouth!

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.700
I wonder if Azuma’s eating his meals properly...

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.290
Good morning.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.950
Let’s work hard and energetically again today, shall we?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.910
Good morning.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.760
Azuma-kun,

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.720
you look very well today, as well.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.680
Yeah, but it appears that it’s just me.

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:39.930
Tsukino-san!

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.850
Cheer up!

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.020
Tsukino-san, please!

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.800
There’s no help for these people.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.650
Listen up, everybody.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.150
Nothing’s going to come out of being depressed.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.450
I understand that you all feel attached to Pantasia.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:56.320
But, that’s precisely why we should fight!

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.370
This Southern Tokyo Branch is diagonally opposite to St. Pierre’s Main Branch.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.370
Any changes they make can be studied directly here.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.820
This is the perfect environment for us to fight back in.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:10.830
If our activities can somehow lead
to a huge drop in St. Pierre’s sales...

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:11.300
Tsukino-san!

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.050
it’s possible that we could prevent the takeover.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.060
Cheer up!

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:18.180
However, how in the world...?

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.520
Over there, they have many who line up every day.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.810
After Azuma-san and
Mokoyama-san’s match,

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.560
things have been looking up for us a little,

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.320
but there’s no change in the
fact that things are hard for us.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:28.560
That’s all right.

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:31.560
I have an idea.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.700
Good morning, Kawachi-san.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.060
This is your personal workshop, Kawachi-san.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:38.950
Personal?!

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.110
The Main Branch gives a
personal workshop to a mere artisan?!

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.360
This is amazing.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:48.330
If this was the Southern Tokyo Branch, then...

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.080
Oh, sorry. I slipped.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:54.800
You’re in my way!

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.430
Can’t be helped, it’s cramped here!

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:00.580
Every day was filled with things like that.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.590
Compared to that...

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.900
Here, it’s like heaven.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:08.590
That may be true, but...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:20.250
I’ve put St. Pierre’s Main Branch’s customer
information from yesterday into this graph.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.870
Please pay special attention to the sales in the evening.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.750
It’s amazing.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.080
It’s ten times...

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.340
No, twenty times our ability to pull in customers.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.500
Actually, this area is

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.560
located near a road that children from two middle and two high schools use to commute.

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.840
Therefore, we’d expect that during the evening,

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.390
when there are hungry middle
and high school girls returning home,

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:45.730
we should be able to have huge
sales on their favorite sweet breads.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.480
It’s a perfect chance for us!

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.510
Or it should be...

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:53.510
But, that chance has been
completely stolen by St. Pierre.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.020
So, let’s hear this idea of yours.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:02.950
St. Pierre’s big seller, their sweet bread kouign-pudding-amann, is marketed by using

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:07.630
low calorie substitutes such as
black sugar or honey as sweeteners.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.870
With this, they caught the hearts of

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:12.530
high school girls who always complain about their diet.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.760
On the other hand, our big seller, kabukiage bread,

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.600
<i>Japan</i> #57...

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.180
In addition to being free and of no profit,

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:24.980
it’s avoided by young girls, as it’s high in calories.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.610
Therefore...

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.720
Let’s try using this nanshoukasei wheat flour.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:32.100
Hard to digest wheat flour

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.400
This is not a flour that you usually see, is it?

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.280
Just as its name indicates, it’s difficult for humans to digest,

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.040
and it’s a flour that helps in dieting.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.120
Wait just one moment.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:40.140
Hard to digest wheat flour

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.780
Nanshoukasei wheat flour contains
the hard, fibrous component of wheat,

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:48.160
and definitely helps in dieting,
but in exchange,

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.740
it’s hard for gluten to form, which
leads to a dry taste; a great demerit.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:53.960
What?

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:57.710
In that case, wouldn’t it be hard
for us to even knead it into dough?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.470
Yes.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.200
That’s why even the most well
known stores don’t bother with it.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:03.010
You knew that and yet...

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:03.830
you...

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.930
In order to overcome that defect,

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.520
this is an improved product
which I’ve personally developed...

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.520
a special nanshoukasei wheat flour.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.030
With this, we should be fine!

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.490
Is what I thought, but...

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.810
Not even I can knead it.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:26.530
Tsukino-san!

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:27.080
Me, neither.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.830
Look! Look! I can’t, either!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:29.410
I’m no good, either.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:30.410
How about you, Azuma-san?

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:31.820
Tsukino-san, look!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.320
It’s impossible, is it?

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.250
Don’t worry.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.830
It’s not over yet.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.340
That’s right.

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:40.920
There’s sure to be some other way!

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.080
I wonder if there really is...

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:44.940
Thank you.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.580
Saying that it’s a special flour was a complete lie.

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:51.190
I knew that it was impossible...

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:55.610
But for now, it looks like everyone’s spirits are back up.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.070
Next...

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:01.200
I’ll see if I can somehow actually make
an improved nanshoukasei wheat flour...

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.400
However...

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.240
Now that I have neither the facilities nor the funding...

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.710
It’s all right.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:09.080
I can knead it.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.200
What, but just now...

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:11.610
But...

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.110
it’ll take three days.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.250
Don’t tell me he’s planning to
keep kneading it for three days...

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.640
I think it’s pointless...

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.120
Oh my!

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.090
No way!

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:28.510
Right?

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:29.680
Not just me.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:31.300
All of your dough also  firmed up nicely, right?

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:35.300
What kind of trick could have...?

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.810
Well, you know about hie and millet, right?

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:39.860
Y-Yeah.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.570
My Grandpa really likes

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:45.410
bread that has some mixed in, <i>Japan</i> #15,

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:48.810
as it reminds him of his childhood days.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.540
But...

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.790
Besides being hard to knead,
it tastes really dry.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.700
So, it was really unpopular with the rest of my family.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:57.710
So,

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:02.210
since it was dry, I wondered if it’d be softer if I
submerged it in water and left it there for a while.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.760
So, when I covered it with a wrap
and left it in the fridge for a while,

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:06.430
it got nice and soft.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.710
I see! That method is possible!

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.010
It’s autodigestion!

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:11.710
Huh?

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.230
Didn’t we already introduce ourselves?

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:15.440
Oh well, whatever.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.480
I’m Azuma Kazuma. Nice to meet you.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:17.850
That is, in other words...

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:18.860
Actually, my hobbies include making <i>Japan</i>, but...

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.270
When grain with hard fiber is mixed with water

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:24.240
and left at low temperatures
like that inside a refrigerator,

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.700
the grain will start secreting enzymes on its own.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.320
Fermentation will start,
and it’ll become soft.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.230
This process is called autodigestion.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.120
He’s crushing the fool.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:35.730
If Kawachi-san was here, he would’ve made a comical situation out of it.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.540
Nevertheless, I was careless.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.710
It’s not rare to find high class restaurants that can make

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:45.750
high fiber items like celery soft by
soaking it in water for a long time.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.090
Azuma-kun,

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:48.800
you really are a genius!

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:52.930
Scientists like me think too much, and
easily create blind spots for ourselves.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:55.140
Everyone, even if it takes
a little more effort,

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.760
let’s use this flour
in all of our sweet breads.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:01.060
Tsukino-san, could you make the
banner for our advertisement, please?

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.070
Okay.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.730
You with the mushroom head, please
make the posters and distribute them.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.520
W-Who you calling a mushroom head?!

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.000
Moreover, all of a sudden he’s giving orders.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.070
<i>Japan</i>, Hiromi, whatever.
Note: Hiromi is a name. Stupid joke.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.050
But, it appears that the cockroaches have started to make their move.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:29.130
Is it okay to leave them alone, Mr. St. Pierre owner?

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.140
You can call me Kirisaki...

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.080
Miss Soon-To-Be-Pantasia-Owner.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.430
They spark my interest a little.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.090
I want to leave them alone for a bit.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:39.990
Is that so?

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:42.610
But to me, they’re just an eyesore.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:45.050
Should I just blow up the
Southern Tokyo Branch right away, too?

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:48.070
That’s what I mean, Yukino-kun.

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:51.870
Why did you blow up Kanmuri-kun’s research facility?

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.410
He probably doesn’t know this,

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.110
but we provided him with quite
a bit of financial support as well.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.370
Are you complaining about the loss of your investment?

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:00.870
That’s not it.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.960
He’s really smart.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.800
If he betrays us, and an obstacle
appears in our plan, it’ll be troublesome.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:08.560
That’s precisely why I blew it up.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:12.620
The possibility of him betraying us was always there.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.760
At that time,

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:18.810
had he been storing any proof of our plans within the data or something in his laboratory,

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.130
it would’ve been troublesome, right?

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.030
Just as long as there is no evidence...

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:30.330
I’ve dispersed the stock under several hundred names.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:35.320
Nobody can prove that all of them are actually mine.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:37.580
Even if it gets discovered,

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.000
I’m the owner’s granddaughter.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:43.920
All I need to say is that
I bought up the stock

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:46.470
to protect it from St. Pierre by creating a wall.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.630
Grandfather trusts me.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:54.120
The little boy probably understands that it’s useless
trying to expose it without any proof as well.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.630
But, be sure to take care.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.230
You’re such a worry wart.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:04.650
But even then... <i>Japan</i>, is it?

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.640
I guess just about anyone
can come up with the name, eh?

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:11.640
Ridiculous.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.140
I’d like a <i>Japan</i>, please!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.490
Are all of the <i>Japan</i> #15 like this?

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:17.660
Since the shapes are different,

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.910
they might as well call them #11 or #12.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.460
But, in that case, it would be the same
as our clothes sizes and would feel weird.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:24.420
It was really effective.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.150
A woman’s heart is so...

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:29.000
It’s great that so many people
have come, isn’t it, Kawachi?

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:29.840
Kanmuri!

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:30.630
Could I have a moment?

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:31.310
I mixed up the afros.
Could I have a moment?

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.160
I mixed up the afros.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.550
Oh yeah...

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:36.670
He’s not here anymore.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:41.170
Kanmuri, what’s your true objective?

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:47.190
It’s true that our sales have improved thanks to you.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.190
However...

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:50.430
Someone like you can’t seriously be thinking

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:55.500
that something like this could
prevent St. Pierre’s takeover.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.370
It’s a really wild plan, so...

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:03.440
I thought that I’d talk about it after I
gained a little more of your trust, but...

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.040
For now...

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.400
I’ll tell just you, Manager...

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.930
My true objective.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:15.410
The Monaco Cup is going to take
place during their study abroad in France...

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:19.140
It’s to have Japan representatives...

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:22.670
earn ten billion yen over there.

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:25.420
Ten billion, you say?!

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.270
What’s this?

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:30.970
I come back after a while to find you

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.620
talking of quite a big plan here.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:40.900
Won’t you let me in on this plan as well?

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:52.280
Won’t you let me in on this plan as well?

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:05.890
Kawachi!

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:06.320
Kawachi-san!
Kawachi!

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:06.800
Kawachi-san!

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:09.300
Why?

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:19.280
Kawachi-san!

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.020
It’s Kawachi!
Kawachi-san!

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.020
I can’t take this anymore!

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.910
To think that it was a wig...

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:26.960
How could it be anything
other than a wig?

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:30.170
I mean, you can’t have an
afro unless you have long hair.

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:33.040
B-But, in order to install yourself with an afro,

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.380
was it necessary to shave yourself bald?

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:36.550
It’s the opposite.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.840
Since I really didn’t want an afro, the nun in that church

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:42.260
forcefully used the clippers on me instead.

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:45.600
However, a skin head’s embarrassing, right?

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.610
So, I thought that it had to be an
afro until my hair grew back a little.

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.050
T-There’s no meaning to it.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.550
So, what brings you here today then, Kawachi?

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:59.740
Well... I figured that you all must be lonely without me,

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.200
so I thought that I’d just drop by for a bit...

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.560
and then I heard that
conversation about your big plan...

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.570
In reality, wasn’t it you who was lonely?

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.250
Yay! It’s all bristly. It feels good!

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:10.960
Hey there, Azuma.
Yay! It’s all bristly. It feels good!

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:11.880
You look really happy.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.000
Hey there, don’t play with people’s heads!
Yay! It’s all bristly. It feels good!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.580
Yay! It’s all bristly. It feels good!
Hey there, don’t play with people’s heads!

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.640
So, Kanmuri...

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.300
Continuing with your earlier conversation...

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:22.840
What did you mean when you said that you’d have Japan representatives earn ten billion yen?

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.300
T-T-Ten billion?!

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:27.560
Wow...

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.180
How much longer are you going to do that?!

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.300
That’s our Kawachi-san!

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:35.280
I had wanted to leave out the details for a while, but...

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:39.160
now that they’ve heard about it,
I have no choice but to tell them, right?

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:42.000
The extra prize of studying abroad in France

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.370
that was given away in the newcomers’ battle a few days ago...

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:48.330
While that’s referred to as “studying abroad,” it doesn’t involve any field trips or tourism.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:49.790
There’s a World Bread Tournament

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.540
that occurs in Monaco for
young bakers under the age of 22.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.820
This prize forces you to enter the Monaco Cup.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:57.960
A world tournament?

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:58.820
What was that?!

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.580
Then, the ten billion that you were
talking about is the championship prize?

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:04.090
Of course not.

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:06.140
Not even the world renowned

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:09.290
Bakery World Cup has that kind of prize money.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.100
The Monaco Cup is

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:16.560
a bread tournament that has more than 80 member
nations from the world compete with each other,

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:19.070
and you can bet on who the championship team will be

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:21.310
in Monaco’s Grand Casino as well.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.490
As you know,

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:27.280
the Kingdom of Monaco gains enormous earnings
from its support of state-managed casinos.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.790
Therefore, it’s a country in which taxes do not exist.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.800
Therefore, the bread tournament is...?

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:34.320
You must have guessed by now, right?

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.800
My true objective is to bet on the championship team,

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.630
that is, on the team from Japan,

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:43.170
earn ten billion...

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:45.580
and take over Pantasia once again.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:50.090
Y-You’re saying this seriously?

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.680
I’m really serious.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:55.850
Luckily, Pantasia’s newcomers
were all extremely low level last year.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:57.650
They all failed at the preliminaries.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:59.480
Most likely, in this tournament,

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:02.060
there’s no one who’d predict that Japan could win.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:06.500
At the very least, the odds will exceed 100 to 1.

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:09.160
I guess I’m just one of those low-level newcomers

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.630
who failed last year at the preliminaries.

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:14.380
I understand what you’re aiming for, but...

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.210
if we lose...

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:18.290
we’ll lose everything.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:22.140
If you believe that there’s
any other way, I’d like to hear it.

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:25.340
We don’t need to do something so dangerous.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:29.100
If we just talk to Grandfather,
I’m sure that my sister’s...

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:31.130
That Yukino’s scheme can be...

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:33.590
Are you saying that seriously?

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.190
If that woman could be
crushed with just something like that,

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.060
I’d have done so
from the very beginning.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:41.140
You know this best of all, don’t you?

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.110
It’s true that your grandfather,

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.290
the owner Azusagawa, is good enough
at management to be considered a god.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:49.240
However,

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:52.290
when it comes to his granddaughters,
he becomes completely spineless.

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.610
He becomes a regular old man.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:56.150
After being at that woman’s side, I know this well.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.580
Even if we expose the fact that she’s buying up stock...

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.670
she’d say that it’s just the owner’s
granddaughter buying the stock, after all,

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.660
and he won’t think that anything’s strange.

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:08.090
I really want that woman to get what she deserves.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.690
And I’ll show you how determined I am
to make sure she does get it now.

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:12.890
Because of her...

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:14.670
I lost everything.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:20.320
Tsukino-san... it’s time you got
your act together and braced yourself.

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:22.680
If we don’t stop her,

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:26.680
someone will get hurt again.

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:33.400
There is ten million yen here.

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:37.440
All the money from my research that I’ve saved is here.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:40.830
It’s the first time I’ve seen so
many zeroes all together...

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.420
I’ll donate this money to the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.890
I’ll leave the manager, Matsushiro-san, to decide how this will be used.

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:50.160
Very well.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:54.720
However, even with this,
we’re low on funds.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:56.850
We need everyone’s cooperation.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:20:00.170
In order to save Pantasia, the
Japan representatives just have to...

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.450
Don’t worry.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:05.150
I don’t quite understand the difficult stuff,

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:07.440
but all we have to do is win, right?

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.030
What are you saying?!

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.570
We’re up against the world!

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:13.140
Not just Pantasia newcomers... It’s the world!

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:15.580
It’s just as Kawachi-san said.

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:19.250
The Monaco Cup is a world tournament where the elite from all over the world gather.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.280
Going like we always have...

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:21.570
That’s why!

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:23.820
That’s precisely why I...

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.510
want to fight it out with those amazing people.

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.820
The Monaco Cup is in a month.

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:47.640
Azuma-kun and everyone’s
study abroad begins next week.

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:52.640
I request that you make your decision by then.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:05.250
It’s true that if we win,
it’d be like a dream come true...

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.960
But... ten billion!

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.160
That number’s so big,
it just doesn’t quite sink in.

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:12.560
What should we do?

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.170
Kawachi-san.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:28.530
Earlier, I said that I’d have the
Japanese team earn ten billion.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:30.680
But, what is truly essential is probably...

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:33.600
your presence, Kawachi-san!

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:38.080
What... Is that so?

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.500
That’s why you gave me the
studying abroad in France prize...

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.080
In other words, after directly battling me,

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:45.610
you figured out my strength!

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:47.110
Not at all.

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:48.660
Why is it always so?!

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:52.510
The really strong one is Azuma-kun.
Suwabara-san is good, too.

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:56.680
But, during the exhibition that determines the odds,

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:58.720
we need you to pretend to be weak,

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:01.140
thus amplifying the chances of the Japanese team.

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:04.280
Therefore, a very important role awaits you!

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:05.390
What was that?!

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.590
So, it’s like I’m just a clown?!

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:12.080
Do you want to work at a
company where Yukino’s the director?

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:15.910
Don’t worry.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:18.610
If it’s you, you can become it.

00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:21.040
The World’s Best Clown.

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:22.860
The Ten Billion Yen Clown!

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:26.920
The Ten Billion Yen Clown?!

00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:56.140
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:58.260
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:00.260
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:01.560
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:04.480
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:06.270
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:08.060
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.160
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:21.040
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:23.080
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.490
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:29.290
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:31.130
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:36.680
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.610 --> 00:23:57.490
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:07.750
Azuma fights to protect Pantasia.

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:11.380
The attack of the St. Pierre
bakers, nicknamed the Dark Third Years,

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:13.390
was simply intense.

00:24:13.390 --> 00:24:15.080
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:17.410
Close Attack!!
The birth of the Black <i>Japan</i>!

00:24:17.410 --> 00:24:19.890
Will you be able to survive it?

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:22.640
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:25.250
Those of you who believe that
you’ll grow fat from eating bread!

00:24:25.250 --> 00:24:26.630
We recommend bread made with rye wheat.

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:29.630
Compared to wheat flour, the rise in blood sugar levels after eating rye flour is low.

00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:31.620
It is more difficult for it to be stored as fat.

00:24:32.050 --> 00:24:33.810
Really?!
